## Result up front

The bounded two-event bridge is positive.

A complete old radial Record `(f,b_1)` can act as an orthogonal classical
control without being overwritten. On a supplied star of six fresh 32-site
Blank blocks, it prepares one new six-qubit live state and one Ready pointer in
direction `f`. The Block22 writer then produces the second permanent radial
Record. The complete factorized construction gives

\[
 \Pr(b_1,b_2\mid\rho,f)
 =\operatorname{Tr}(\rho E_{b_1})T(b_2\mid b_1),
 \qquad
 T(b'\mid b)=\operatorname{Tr}(E_{b'}\rho_b).            \tag{1}
\]

All 1,176 reachable branches are explicit. Their effects normalize, retain the
first-event marginal, and remain normalized when tensored with an arbitrary
external reference. The old classical Record projectors are QND under the
preparation channel. Coherences between distinct valid Record words are
dephased; no full coherent-code-QND claim is made.

This is a meaningful program advance, not a TOE closure. It joins one
permanent Record to a second normalized Record-formation event on explicit
qubit substrate. It does not generate that substrate, produce event three,
define a rate or clock, join an action/source current, or couple to gravity.
