## Fixed 224-site geometry

The Block22 local support has six live sites and twenty-six radial pointer
sites:

```text
S = live union front union axis-outcome union corner-outcome union status,
|S| = 6 + 6 + 6 + 8 + 6 = 32.
```

Let the old anchor be `x=0`, let
`D={+-e_1,+-e_2,+-e_3}`, and put

\[
 y_f=x+9f,\qquad f\in D.                                \tag{2}
\]

The seven translated blocks `S+x` and `S+y_f` are pairwise disjoint. Their
union has 224 sites and radius 13. The set is invariant under all 24 proper
cubic rotations. Each successor block begins in an explicitly supplied pure
radial product `Blank`; the six-block product is `BlankStar_x`.

This BlankStar is finite boundary content. The construction neither creates
nor replenishes it.

## Record-controlled live preparation

For outcome label `b`, let `u_b=b/||b||` and define

\[
 Q_b=u_bu_b^{\mathsf T}-{I_3\over3},\qquad
 v_n(b)={Q_bn\over\lVert Q_bn\rVert},\qquad
 \rho_b=\bigotimes_{n\in D}{I+v_n(b)\cdot\sigma\over2}. \tag{3}
\]

The sign in (3) is load-bearing, while `Q_{-b}=Q_b`. Every local Bloch vector
is unit length and the family transforms under the same onsite spin action as
the radial pointer factors.

Let `C_(f,b)` be the old twenty-six-pointer projector for the complete Locked
word `(f,b)`. Define `Target_(f,b)` to contain

- `rho_b` and `Ready_f` in the block at `y_f`; and
- the exact original Blank product in the other five successor blocks.

The preparation branches are

\[
 A_{f,b}=C_{f,b}\otimes I_{\rm old\ live}
 \otimes|Target_{f,b}\rangle\langle BlankStar_x|.        \tag{4}
\]

Their input effects form the orthogonal projector

\[
 P_{\rm valid}=\sum_{f,b}C_{f,b}\otimes I_{\rm old\ live}
 \otimes|BlankStar_x\rangle\langle BlankStar_x|.         \tag{5}
\]

With

\[
 K_{\rm STOP}=I-P_{\rm valid},                           \tag{6}
\]

orthogonality gives `P_valid^2=P_valid` and hence

\[
 \sum_{f,b}A_{f,b}^\dagger A_{f,b}
 +K_{\rm STOP}^\dagger K_{\rm STOP}=I.                  \tag{7}
\]

Every factor in (4) is an identity, normalized projector, or normalized
rank-one map. Equations (5)--(7) therefore define a global CPTP preparation
channel. Tensoring every Kraus operator with `I_R` gives the same Gram identity
for arbitrary reference indices, not only for a sampled reference dimension.

## Classical-Record QND and covariance

For any old Locked projector `C_k`, its one matching branch contributes
`C_k tensor B`, where `B` is the BlankStar projector. The STOP complement
contributes `C_k tensor (I-B)`. Thus

\[
 \Lambda^\dagger(C_k)=C_k\otimes B+C_k\otimes(I-B)=C_k.  \tag{8}
\]

All 84 projectors satisfy (8), and every old pointer output equals its input.
For distinct valid words `j!=k`, no single indexed Kraus branch accepts both
controls and STOP annihilates both Blank-domain inputs. Their matrix unit is
therefore dephased exactly. The result preserves the classical Record algebra,
not arbitrary coherent superpositions of different Record words.

Rotating input controls, all 192 Blank/target factors, and output controls by
one proper cubic frame sends the `(f,b)` branch CP map to `(gf,gb)`. Separate
Kraus indexing is essential; no coherent sum across front sectors is used.

## Factorized two-event composition

For a fixed supplied `Ready_f tensor BlankStar_x` input domain, one composite
branch contains:

1. the first 64-sector spectral root `sqrt(E_b1)`;
2. twenty-six `Ready_f -> Locked_(f,b1)` pointer maps;
3. the Record-controlled preparation (4), with six old-live identities and all
   192 star rank-one factors;
4. the second root `sqrt(E_b2)` on the explicitly identified block `y_f`;
5. twenty-six `Ready_f -> Locked_(f,b2)` maps in that block; and
6. five identity STOP actions on the other Blank blocks.

The runner contracts `M^dagger M` from those stored factors. It does not assign
the expected transition table to the branch. The contraction gives the full
conditional-domain effect

\[
 M_{f,b_1,b_2}^\dagger M_{f,b_1,b_2}
 =E_{b_1}T(b_2\mid b_1)\otimes
 |Ready_f\rangle\langle Ready_f|\otimes
 |BlankStar_x\rangle\langle BlankStar_x|.                \tag{9}
\]

The expected right side is then an independent comparison. Summing (9) over
`b_2` returns `E_b1`; summing over both outcomes returns identity on the old
live algebra, conditional on the displayed Ready/Blank domain. A symbolic
Kronecker-delta calculation proves the same identity after tensoring with an
arbitrary reference.

Equation (9) is not a claim that the reachable branch family is a global
channel on every pointer and star input. The preparation map itself is global
CPTP; the two-event prefix theorem is deliberately conditional on the supplied
Ready and Blank sectors.

## Exact internal transition kernel

For an axis source ray `a`, the signed transition probabilities are

```text
target +a or -a:             1/9 each
other signed axis target:    5/72 each
any corner target:           1/16.
```

For a corner source `c`, they are

```text
any signed axis target:      1/12
corner target +c or -c:      1/16 + 3/(64 sqrt(2))
other corner target:         1/16 - 1/(64 sqrt(2)).
```

All 196 entries are strictly positive and each row sums to one. Antipodal
lumping gives seven rays with

```text
axis diagonal:               2/9
axis off-diagonal:           5/36
axis to corner:              1/8
corner to axis:              1/6
corner diagonal:             1/8 + 3/(32 sqrt(2))
corner off-diagonal:         1/8 - 1/(32 sqrt(2)).
```

The signed stationary weights are `1/12` per axis label and `1/16` per corner
label; the ray weights are `1/6` and `1/8`. Detailed balance holds exactly. The
seven-ray spectrum is

\[
 1,\quad0,\quad(1/12)^{\times2},\quad(\sqrt2/16)^{\times3}. \tag{10}
\]

This is an internal outcome kernel. Keeping the front label gives six closed
42-state sectors, the physical anchor drifts, and permanent append is
irreversible. Nothing here establishes a stationary or reversible spatial
Record process.

## Exact event-three boundary

After the second event at `y_f`, literal reuse of the same successor-star rule
examines centers

\[
 z_d=y_f+9d,\qquad d\in D.                              \tag{11}
\]

For the backward direction,

\[
 z_{-f}=x,\qquad S+z_{-f}=S+x.                           \tag{12}
\]

That support is the old Locked block, not a Blank block. The other five
candidate 32-site supports are pairwise disjoint and are disjoint from the
entire supplied 224-site domain. They are therefore **unsupplied/unknown**, not
realized Blanks.

Consequently the exact all-six-Blank projector used in (4) annihilates this
realized predecessor sector and cannot be directly reused to append event
three. This is only an architecture-specific predicate failure. It does not
exclude a projector that explicitly accepts one backward Locked predecessor,
nor a law that supplies or owns the other five blocks, reroutes the front, or
arbitrates a general occupied neighborhood.

The highest-value next theorem is therefore concrete: construct a third-event
channel with one typed backward Locked block and five explicitly available
candidate blocks, preserve both earlier Records, and prove the three-event
cylinder plus both prefix marginals.

